Lucciola: the typed password follows the conversation to another output

Each output has its own password field, and with start_on_select (patch
0002) the greetd conversation moves to the output in use: when the
pointer enters another output, or when the output it was on is
unplugged. The field's text did not move with it. A password typed on
one output then stayed in that output's field, and Enter on the new one
found an empty field: at PAM's password prompt that is 0002's empty
Enter, which starts the conversation over (the reader listens again)
instead of logging in; while the reader waits it kept nothing; after an
unplug the typed text was gone.

The text now goes where the conversation goes (handOverAuthTo) and, with
no conversation running, where the keyboard goes (setActiveSurface): the
field on the new output gets it, replacing whatever it held, and the old
one is emptied, so the field in use is the only one that holds the
password. With the key off nothing changes.

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.6.0 tag,
after 0004. Could be proposed upstream together with 0002.

